        "text": "The great benefit of blockchain is that there's no central authority that everyone needs to trust for the system to work. This means that a blockchain can act as a single source of truth in the digital world. It allows a network of users to agree on what the database contains and to synchronize any new updates. The peer to peer architecture of blockchains is made of a distributed network of users, each having equal rights. Updates don't need to go through a central coordinator. Every user on this network downloads blocks from others in order to create their own copy of the database.",
